A capital Greek letter is upright by default.  The forms with var
({c:\varGamma} and the others) are the slanted capitals; {c:\boldsymbol} ({n:eq-fonts}) makes any of them bold.

.h2 Binary operators [eq-binary]
.ix Binary operators
A binary operator is a sign that stands between two things, as the plus sign
does.  TeX puts a medium space on both sides of it, unless it stands at the
start of the formula or follows another operator or a relation, in which case
it is a sign of one operand (compare {eq:a-b} with {eq:-b}).  To have the sign
without spaces, put it in a group ({c:a{{+}}b}, {n:eq-spacing}).  The signs
that are marked amssymb are less usual ones.

