To make a symbol that is not an operator behave like one, use {c:\mathbin}
({n:eq-spacing}).

.h2 Relations [eq-relations]
.ix Relations
A relation is a sign that says how two things stand to each other, such as the
equals sign.  TeX puts a thick space on both sides of it.  The negation of a
relation is made by putting {c:\not} in front of the command: {eq:\not\equiv}.
Many relations have a ready made negation ({c:\neq}, {c:\notin}, {c:\nless}
and others), which is better set than {c:\not}.  The relations that are marked
amssymb are less usual ones.

