.end

A vertical bar typed on the keyboard is the vertical line.  Use {c:\lvert} and
{c:\rvert} for absolute values (they have the right spacing) and {c:\lVert}
and {c:\rVert} for norms.

.h2 Accents, lines and braces [eq-accents]
.ix Accents, lines and braces
An accent is a command with one argument, the letter that gets it.  Accents
over several letters ({c:\widehat}, {c:\widetilde}, {c:\overline}, the braces)
stretch.  The arrows that stretch over text and take a label are
{c:\xrightarrow} and {c:\xleftarrow}, which have the label as an argument, and
a second label under the arrow in square brackets.

