 height and depth
.end

Bold Greek letters need {c:\boldsymbol}: {c:\mathbf} leaves the Greek letters
as they are.  The letters of {c:\mathcal} and of {c:\mathbb} are meant for
capitals (the small letters of them are not the ones wanted); {c:\mathfrak}
has both cases.

.h2 Spacing [eq-spacing]
.ix Spacing
TeX makes the space of a formula from the kind of each sign: an ordinary sign
(a letter, a digit) has none, an operator has a medium space on both sides, a
relation a thick space, a comma a thin space after it.  The spaces that you
type are ignored.  To change the result there are fixed spaces ({c:\,}, {c:\:},
{c:\;}, {c:\quad}, {c:\qquad}), a negative space ({c:\!}), and commands that
blank an area of the size of their argument ({c:\phantom}, {c:\hphantom},
{c:\vphantom}). {c:\mathbin}, {c:\mathrel}, {c:\mathop}, {c:\mathopen},
{c:\mathclose}, {c:\mathord}, {c:\mathpunct} and {c:\mathinner} tell TeX what
kind of sign the argument is, and so which space it gets. {c:\hspace} and
{c:\vspace} are refused in a printed equation ({n:eq-refused}).

.table 25 15 18
Source | Result | Meaning
{c:a\,b} | {eq:a\,b} | thin space (3/18 em)
{c:a\:b} | {eq:a\:b} | medium space (4/18 em)
{c:a\;b} | {eq:a\;b} | thick space (5/18 em)
{c:a\!b} | {eq:a\!b} | negative thin space
{c:a\ b} | {eq:a\ b} | space of the text font
{c:a\quad b} | {eq:a\quad b} | one em
{c:a\qquad b} | {eq:a\qquad b} | two em
{c:a \thinspace b} | {eq:a \thinspace b} | thin space, the TeX name
{c:a \medspace b} | {eq:a \medspace b} | medium space, the amsmath name
{c:a \thickspace b} | {eq:a \thickspace b} | thick space, the amsmath name
{c:a \negthinspace b} | {eq:a \negthinspace b} | negative thin space, the TeX
 name
{c:a \negmedspace b} | {eq:a \negmedspace b} | negative medium space
{c:a \negthickspace b} | {eq:a \negthickspace b} | negative thick space
