{c:a{{+}}b} | {eq:a{{+}}b} | a group makes the sign ordinary: no spaces
{c:a+b} | {eq:a+b} | the spaces are made by the sign
{c:a = b} | {eq:a = b} | the spaces that you type are ignored
.end

Between the integral and the differential use the thin space {c:\,}: {eq:\int
f(x)\,dx} against {eq:\int f(x)dx}.

.h2 Matrices, arrays and alignment [eq-structures]
.ix Matrices, arrays and alignment
The environments are begun with {c:\begin{{name}}} and ended with
{c:\end{{name}}}; a row ends with two backslashes, and the cells of a row are
separated by the sign &. The environments that are allowed in a printed
equation are matrix, pmatrix, bmatrix, Bmatrix, vmatrix, Vmatrix, cases,
array, aligned, gathered, split, smallmatrix and subarray; any other name
makes the equation print in the long form ({n:eq-refused}).  The name split is
on the list but is no use: it needs a displayed formula of amsmath round it,
which an equation of Strata does not have, and TeX stops with the message
"Package amsmath Error: {c:\begin}{{split}} won't work here"; use aligned in
its place.  The matrix environments have no column specification: every column
is centered. {c:array} has one, a letter for each column: c, l or r, and a bar
for a vertical rule. {c:\hline} draws a horizontal rule. {c:aligned} aligns
the rows at the sign & (an & before the sign), and {c:gathered} centers them.
{c:cases} is a brace with a column of values and a column of conditions.  The
results are set in display size.

The tables of this group typeset the result as {x:eq-scripts} says.

.table 25 15 18
Source | Result | Meaning
{c:\begin{{matrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{matrix}}} | {eq:\displaystyle
 \begin{{matrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{matrix}}} | matrix, no delimiters
{c:\begin{{pmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{pmatrix}}} | {eq:\displaystyle
 \begin{{pmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{pmatrix}}} | matrix in parentheses
{c:\begin{{bmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{bmatrix}}} | {eq:\displaystyle
 \begin{{bmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{bmatrix}}} | matrix in square brackets
{c:\begin{{Bmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{Bmatrix}}} | {eq:\displaystyle
 \begin{{Bmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{Bmatrix}}} | matrix in braces
{c:\begin{{vmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{vmatrix}}} | {eq:\displaystyle
 \begin{{vmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{vmatrix}}} | determinant bars
{c:\begin{{Vmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{Vmatrix}}} | {eq:\displaystyle
 \begin{{Vmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{Vmatrix}}} | norm bars
{c:\begin{{smallmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{smallmatrix}}} |
 {eq:\displaystyle \begin{{smallmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{smallmatrix}}} |
 small matrix for a line of text
{c:\left(\begin{{smallmatrix}} a & b \\ c & d \end{{smallmatrix}}\right)} |
